Restaurant QR Menu SaaS — Architecture Summary & Implementation Plan
This is a well-thought-out specification for a multi-tenant restaurant QR menu + ordering SaaS. Here's a consolidated breakdown with practical implementation guidance.

Core Concept
A multi-restaurant SaaS where each restaurant gets:

A unique QR code → public server-rendered menu

Their own admin panel for menu/order management

Theme customization without code changes

Cash-on-Delivery ordering

You (the SaaS owner) get a super admin panel to manage all tenants.

Key Architectural Decisions
Decision	Choice	Why
Rendering	Server-rendered EJS (not React/Next)	Speed for public menu, simpler stack
Multi-tenancy	Shared DB, restaurant_id on every table	Simplest to maintain, scales fine
URL strategy	yourmenu.com/r/:slug → later custom domains	MVP simplicity → premium upsell
Caching	Redis for menu/settings	Invalidate on admin change
Images	Sharp → WebP/AVIF, 3 sizes	Mobile performance
Auth	JWT + HTTP-only cookies	Standard, secure
DB	PostgreSQL + proper indexes	Handles thousands of restaurants/items
Critical Rules (Don't Skip)
1. Tenant Isolation Is Non-Negotiable
Every query for restaurant-owned data must filter by restaurant_id. Never trust an ID from the URL alone.

js
// WRONG
const item = await db.query('SELECT * FROM menu_items WHERE id = $1', [id]);

// RIGHT
const item = await db.query(
  'SELECT * FROM menu_items WHERE id = $1 AND restaurant_id = $2',
  [id, req.tenant.restaurantId]
);
2. Never Hardcode Colors/Theme
Store theme config in DB → emit CSS variables:

html
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: {{ theme.primary_color }};
    --radius: {{ theme.border_radius }}px;
    --font: {{ theme.font_family }};
  }
</style>
3. Image Pipeline
text
Upload → Multer → Sharp → {thumb 300, medium 600, large 1000} in WebP
Serve thumb/medium in listings, large in detail modal. Always loading="lazy" below fold.

4. Cache Menu Aggressively
text
Customer → Nginx → Node → Redis → Postgres (only on miss)
Invalidate key restaurant:{id}:menu when admin edits categories/items/settings.

Database Schema (Starter)
text
users                  (super admins, restaurant admins)
restaurants            (id, name, slug, theme_id, status, ...)
restaurant_settings    (colors, button_style, font, radius)
themes                 (modern | elegant | classic)
categories             (id, restaurant_id, parent_id, sort_order)
menu_items             (id, restaurant_id, category_id, price, ...)
item_options           (add-ons: cheese, egg, etc.)
item_option_values     (price per option)
item_images            (multiple per item, sizes)
customers              (guest-created on first order)
customer_addresses
orders                 (id, restaurant_id, table_id, type, status)
order_items
order_item_options
restaurant_tables      (for QR-per-table)
qr_codes
coupons
Essential indexes:

sql
CREATE INDEX idx_menu_items_restaurant_category
  ON menu_items(restaurant_id, category_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_orders_restaurant_created
  ON orders(restaurant_id, created_at DESC);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_restaurants_slug ON restaurants(slug);
Project Structure (Node + Express + EJS)
text
src/
├── config/        (database.js, redis.js)
├── controllers/   (admin/, restaurant/, customer/, auth/)
├── routes/
├── services/      (menu, order, restaurant, image, cache)
├── repositories/  (SQL lives here, not in routes)
├── middleware/    (auth, tenant, validation)
├── validators/
└── utils/

views/
├── admin/
├── restaurant/
├── customer/
└── themes/{modern,elegant,classic}/

public/  (css, js, images, fonts)
uploads/
migrations/
seeds/
server.js
Layering: Route → Controller → Service → Repository → Postgres/Redis

Never write 300-line SQL blobs in a route handler.

Three Panels to Build
1. Super Admin (/admin)
Restaurant CRUD (create, activate, suspend)

Assign theme + button style

Reset restaurant admin passwords

View global stats: restaurants, items, orders, revenue

Generate / download QR codes

Subscription management (later)

2. Restaurant Admin (/dashboard)
Today's stats: pending / preparing / completed / cancelled

Menu builder: Categories → Subcategories → Items (parent_id based)

Item editor: name, price, discount, image, add-ons, badges (spicy, veg, best-seller)

Order queue with status transitions

Appearance: pick theme + colors + button shape

3. Customer Menu (/r/:slug)
Landing: logo, cover, search, horizontal category chips

Product grid → tap → bottom-sheet modal with add-ons + quantity

Cart via fetch (no page reload), animated count badge

Checkout: guest name/phone/address, dine-in/takeaway/delivery

COD only for MVP

Table auto-detected from ?table=04 if QR-per-table

QR Flow
text
/r/bbq-tonight              → general menu
/r/bbq-tonight?table=04     → dine-in, table pre-filled
bbq-tonight.yourmenu.com    → custom domain (post-MVP)
Security Checklist
□ Argon2/bcrypt password hashing
□ HTTP-only + Secure + SameSite cookies
□ CSRF tokens on state-changing forms
□ Rate limiting (especially on login, order creation)
□ Helmet.js
□ Parameterized SQL everywhere
□ Multer file-size + MIME validation
□ Role-based middleware (super_admin, restaurant_admin, customer)
□ Tenant middleware resolves req.tenant from slug/domain
□ Order ownership check on every order fetch
Performance Targets
Metric	Target
Menu TTFB (cached)	< 100ms
Menu TTFB (uncached)	< 400ms
First Contentful Paint	< 1.2s on 4G
Image payload per card	< 40KB (WebP thumb)
JS bundle for menu	< 30KB (vanilla or Alpine.js)
Avoid: React, video backgrounds, 3D, heavy animation libs on the public menu.

Animations (Keep It Subtle)
Product card: fade + 8px translate-up on scroll-in

Add-to-bag button: 100ms scale pulse

Cart badge: slide + count tween

Product modal: scale 0.96→1 + fade, 200ms

Category chips: smooth horizontal scroll snap

SaaS Pricing Tiers (Suggested)
Tier	Features
Free	QR menu, 1 basic theme, 50 items, no orders
Basic	Unlimited items, 3 themes, orders, analytics
Pro	Custom domain, coupons, multi-branch, multi-staff, featured items, advanced analytics
Roadmap Suggestion
Phase 1 (MVP)

DB schema + migrations

Super admin: create restaurant, assign slug + theme

Restaurant admin: category + item CRUD with image upload

Customer menu: SSR list + item modal + cart + COD checkout

QR generation

Order appears in restaurant admin

Phase 2

Redis caching, image variants (thumb/medium/large WebP)

Table-specific QRs

Coupons, featured items, add-ons

Customer accounts + order history

Phase 3

Custom domains

Multi-branch per restaurant

Analytics dashboard

Subscription billing

Payment gateways (JazzCash, Easypaisa, Stripe)





